WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:02.980
- [Narrator] One of Hollywood's
recent breakout stars

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.930
isn't some up-and-coming actor.

00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.020
Actually, he isn't even human.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.400
It's this little guy, Baby Yoda,

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.190
or that's what fans named
the child-like alien

00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:14.930
from the hit Disney+
show, The Mandalorian.

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.160
Instantly meme-able, the
little green character

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.750
helped make Disney's new show

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.120
and its new streaming
platform a smash hit.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:24.610
Since launching in November 2019,

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:27.040
Disney+ has surged to the upper echelon

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.770
of the crowded streaming ranks,

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.170
with 37 million subscribers in the US

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:33.350
and over 86 million globally.

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.730
It's success has marked
a bright spot for Disney,

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.530
a company that has lost
a little bit of magic.

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.100
In The Mandalorian,
characters go to great lengths

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.033
and take a few risks
to keep Baby Yoda safe.

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.010
(dramatic music)

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:48.730
And in many ways, Disney
has made similar moves

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:51.483
to help its nascent
streaming platform thrive.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.260
Baby Yoda might have been a new character,

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.700
but the universe he lives
in wasn't new at all.

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.960
Disney owns the Star Wars franchise.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:01.860
It's one of the many well-known brands

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:05.000
the company packed into its
Disney+ streaming catalog.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.990
WSJ's Eric Schwartzel has been
following Disney+'s growth.

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:12.170
- The Mandalorian has been
the breakout hit of Disney+

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.360
and it's no surprise because it combines

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:18.450
a known entity, the Star Wars universe,

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:22.120
arguably the most successful
franchise in Hollywood history,

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.790
with a new storyline that you can only see

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:27.060
and explore on Disney+.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.020
- [Narrator] Disney+ offered 500 films

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.350
and over 7,500 TV episodes at launch.

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:35.060
- They had this stable of brands

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.580
that they could already draw on.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:38.940
Plus, they had movies and characters

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.290
that people wanted to
watch again and again.

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:44.540
So if Disney+ became the exclusive home

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:48.380
of the Iron Man movies and
the Finding Nemo movies,

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.130
that was already a built-in advantage.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:52.360
Then they were able to use
those brands and characters

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:56.170
to make sequels and
reboots that become events

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:59.010
on the service and give
them this perfect bridge

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:02.940
of new material using
older familiar characters.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.040
- [Narrator] This helped
garner 10 million subscribers

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.190
on its first day, with The Mandalorian

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:09.080
driving buzz and aclaim.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.100
This overnight success couldn't have come

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.810
at a better time for Disney.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.490
Even before the pandemic,
investors had questioned

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.850
Disney's longterm growth potential.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:20.080
Disney+ was viewed as a critical venture

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:23.740
to help the company capitalize
on digital entertainment,

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.240
but with so many streaming
options crowding the space,

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.750
the platform wasn't a surefire bet.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:31.910
Here's former Disney CEO and
current executive chairman

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:36.000
Bob Iger speaking to WSJ in 2019.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.580
- This is a dramatic shift

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:41.270
in the way people consume
entertainment and information.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.930
Your business is going
through the same thing.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:48.930
And it requires an
immediate shift in strategy

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:52.650
in order to stay healthy,
in order to thrive.

00:02:52.650 --> 00:02:55.030
- Investors were looking
at companies like Netflix

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:57.240
and seeing those as companies

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.650
where there was a lot of growth,

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.970
whereas Disney, despite
ruling the box office

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:04.460
and having theme parks that
had to turn people away

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:08.120
they were so popular, had a
major issue with cord cutting.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.700
- [Narrator] This cord
cutting was felt most

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:12.620
by Disney-owned cable network, ESPN.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:14.610
And as cable subscriptions fell,

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.710
Disney's stock price became more volatile.

00:03:17.620 --> 00:03:19.630
- Wall Street wanted to see a strategy

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.630
for growth and a strategy for the future.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:24.570
And that is what led
executives to conceive

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:28.240
of Disney+ and launch it in 2019.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.440
So when the pandemic hit with
Disney shuttering theme parks

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.710
and no theaters open to screen movies,

00:03:33.710 --> 00:03:35.240
its share price took a dive.

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.410
With people staying home revenue shrunk

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:39.750
and Disney+ quickly became more important

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.670
to the company's bottom line.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:44.610
- Without those traditional
revenue streams,

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:47.140
Disney+ was leaned on even harder

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.930
as a place to look to for investors

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.410
as something that might
keep the company afloat.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:55.190
And frankly it has worked incredibly well.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:56.830
- [Narrator] So well that Disney announced

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:59.170
a massive restructuring of the company,

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.920
positioning streaming as a top priority.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.770
- Essentially, what we want to do is

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:08.470
separate out the folks who
make our wonderful content

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:11.800
based on tremendous franchises
from the decision-making

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.500
in terms of where the prioritization is,

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.810
in terms of how it gets
commercialized into the marketplace.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:20.360
- [Narrator] This included
redirecting high-profile releases

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:23.704
like Hamilton and Mulan from
theaters onto its platform.

00:04:23.704 --> 00:04:27.558
♪ Alexander Hamilton ♪

00:04:27.558 --> 00:04:30.610
♪ My name is Alexander Hamilton ♪

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:32.780
- They reorganized the company in a way

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:36.230
such that there is now
an almost agnosticism

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:39.820
about where a movie or TV show will run.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:42.370
It is more about creating that show,

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:45.030
building that programming,
and then deciding

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:46.450
would this be best in a theater?

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:48.190
Would this be best on a TV network?

00:04:48.190 --> 00:04:50.170
Would this be best on Disney+?

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:53.470
And increasingly Disney+
is the preferred option.

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:54.610
- [Narrator] This strategy seems

00:04:54.610 --> 00:04:56.360
to have energized Wall Street.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:00.040
Despite posting two consecutive
quarters of losses in 2020,

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:03.358
including losing over $2
billion in its park division,

00:05:03.358 --> 00:05:05.969
Disney's stock price has rebounded.

00:05:05.969 --> 00:05:08.230
In November it announced plans to lay off

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:11.440
32,000 employees by March, 2021,

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:13.490
mostly in its parks division.

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:16.190
It also said it would be
suspending its January dividend

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:18.380
to invest more heavily in streaming.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.570
On top of this Disney+ set of projection

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:23.940
of 260 million subscribers by 2024.

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:25.760
But experts question how realistic

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:28.160
this forecast actually is.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:30.220
A Disney spokesperson said in a statement

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.370
that with a rapidly expanding pipeline

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:35.160
of exceptional original
programming in the works

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.270
the company believes it will significantly

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:40.020
expand its global subscriber base.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.161
- What they're trying
to do now is figure out

00:05:42.161 --> 00:05:44.220
what they can do in terms of pricing

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.790
and also what they can do in
terms of international growth,

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.770
because that is where a lot

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:50.970
of the new subscribers are
going to be coming from.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:52.680
There are some challenges ahead.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:56.010
For one, it remains an
incredibly competitive landscape

00:05:56.010 --> 00:06:00.580
and no one really knows yet
how many streaming services

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.610
the average consumer might
want to subscribe to.

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.760
And the other question
becomes what is temporary

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.890
and what is permanent
when it comes to the way

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:12.210
viewing habits have changed
during the pandemic.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:13.680
- [Narrator] Questions
like these will test

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:14.980
whether Disney can navigate

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:17.410
a post-coronavirus business landscape.

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:20.170
And if Disney+ can not
only be the most magical,

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:22.803
but also the most
streamable place on earth.

